{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And to a woman</b> — two times. One is this, and the other: \"and to a woman in her menstrual impurity you shall not approach\" — and likewise נדת appears twice: here and the other in Ezra — the נדת of the common people, for if he does not approach a menstruating woman, it is written of him: צדיק הוא חיה יחיה (he is righteous, he shall surely live). But if he approaches her during the נדת of her impurity, behold he is in the נדת of the common people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:41.301132268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}